              "className": "SparseChminChmaxAssignMinMaxTree",
              "doc": "Range assign / chmin / chmax with range min / max queries, plus point ops, over any index range [lo, hi] (huge or negative is fine); every position starts at 0. A tag is the map x -> min(hi, max(lo, x + add)), kept as (hi, lo, add); these maps compose into the same form, and each is monotone, so it sends a node's min / max straight to the new min / max. Updates push a node's tag into its children (creating them) before recursing past it; queries never push: they carry the ancestors' tags down and apply them to what they return, so they create no nodes. Sparse: parallel lists of nodes; node 0 is the shared all-zeros block (its sum, min and max are 0 at any length), node 1 is the root.",
